(a) Counties and tribal social services must continue the base level of expenditures for preventive child welfare services from either or both of any state, county, or federal funding source, which, in the absence of federal funds earned under this section, would have been available for these services. The commissioner shall review the county or tribal social services expenditures annually using reports required under sections 245.482 and 256.01, subdivision 2, paragraph [-(p)-][+ (o)+], to ensure that the base level of expenditures for preventive child welfare services is continued from sources other than the federal funds earned under this section.
