Subd. 2.
Definitions.
(a) For the purposes of this section, the terms defined in this subdivision and section [-216B.241, subdivision 1-][+ 216B.2402+], have the meanings given them.
(b) "Eligible renewable energy sources" means fuels and technologies to generate electricity through the use of any of the resources listed in section 216B.1691, subdivision 1, paragraph (c), except that the incineration of wastewater sludge is not an eligible renewable energy source, "biomass" has the meaning provided under paragraph (c), and "solar" must be from a qualified solar energy project as defined in paragraph (d).
